Author: root <root@ns5002569.ip-51-79-162.net>
Date:   Sat Jul 25 18:30:22 2026 +0000

    Per-server disk expansion + portable-volume model

    - Disk expansion: Server.extraDiskGB + DISK_EXPAND job; buy extra root disk at deploy (wizard upsell, priced over the term like the dedicated-IP add-on) or afterwards (prorated wallet/card split, same idempotent Stripe confirm as resize); worker grows the Proxmox disk then the partition + filesystem online; renewals bill it; preserved across plan resize. Growth is ONE-WAY — no shrink path anywhere
    - Volumes stay PORTABLE: LVM pooling deliberately deferred (welding disks together contradicts "attach to any server"); using a volume for /var/lib/docker is now an explicit useVolumeForDocker opt-in (default off) with a "can't detach while in use" warning surfaced in the log and summary; blank-disk detection hardened (children/holders/blkid/4GiB floor), validated live
    - Reinstall now refuses while any volume is pinned to the server — a reinstall purges vm-<vmid>-disk-N and would destroy volume data

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

